From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunuefi-np05j <sunuefi-np05j@local>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0000
Subject: iommu/arm-smmu-qcom: cap stream matching groups to QCOM_HANDOFF_MAX_SMR

Problem:
On nubia NP05J (REDMAGIC Astra, SM8750P), apps_smmu@15000000 reports
ID0=0x4c017e84 (NUMSMRG=132) and ID1=0x60000053 (NUMCB=83). The Piano
firmware DMA handoff patch bounds qcom_smmu_handoff_snapshot to
QCOM_HANDOFF_MAX_SMR (128) and removed mainline's >128 SMR group clamp.
As a result, qcom_smmu_handoff_geometry() rejects num_smr=132 with
-EOPNOTSUPP ("unsupported bounded firmware route geometry"), causing
arm-smmu probe failure (-95) and preventing UFS and all apps_smmu
consumers from probing.

Rationale:
Mainline arm-smmu-qcom already documents that Qualcomm hypervisor
firmware does not reliably trap and emulate stream matching groups
beyond the Arm SMMU architected maximum of 128, and previously clamped
smmu->num_mapping_groups to 128. Applying the same cap to
QCOM_HANDOFF_MAX_SMR (128) before reading live firmware routes keeps
bounded handoff snapshot validation intact and prevents accessing
unemulated SMR/S2CR slots 128..131 during probe or reset.

Verification:
Rebuilt Linux 7.3.3-np05j kernel image for nubia NP05J and verified
clean patch application, build, and on-device boot handoff into UFS
rootfs.
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
index 0ae8efe89985..5f7a2c81b9e4 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
@@ -481,6 +481,19 @@ static int qcom_smmu_cfg_probe(struct arm_smmu_device *smmu)
 			smmu->num_context_banks = 13;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * แพลตฟอร์ม SM8750P (เช่น nubia NP05J) รายงาน NUMSMRG=132 ซึ่งเกิน
+	 * ขีดจำกัดสถาปัตยกรรม ARM SMMU (128) และเกิน QCOM_HANDOFF_MAX_SMR
+	 * ไฮเปอร์ไวเซอร์ของ Qualcomm ไม่ได้จำลองรีจิสเตอร์เกิน 128 อย่างเสถียร
+	 * จึงจำกัดจำนวน SMR ไว้ที่ QCOM_HANDOFF_MAX_SMR ก่อนอ่านเส้นทางเฟิร์มแวร์
+	 */
+	if (smmu->num_mapping_groups > QCOM_HANDOFF_MAX_SMR) {
+		dev_notice(smmu->dev,
+			   "\tLimiting the stream matching groups from %u to %u\n",
+			   smmu->num_mapping_groups, QCOM_HANDOFF_MAX_SMR);
+		smmu->num_mapping_groups = QCOM_HANDOFF_MAX_SMR;
+	}
+
 	/* Read and reserve every live route before probing firmware behaviour.
 	 * A last-slot probe is not safe when firmware occupies that slot, and
 	 * the last CB is not necessarily free even with translation disabled.
